# pico — the EXPECTED listener set, as read live on 2026-08-08 20:25 PT.
#
# Consumed by pico-health.sh check 5. One `bind-address:port` per line; a `#`
# starts a comment. Both directions of the diff are findings: an entry that
# APPEARS here without being listed is an undocumented surface on a box with no
# firewall (ALF and pf both disabled — a wildcard bind is reachable from every
# device on the home LAN), and an entry listed here that has GONE is a service
# that is down. The audit of 2026-08-09 found three listeners nobody had written
# down, two months after they appeared; this file is how the NEXT one is caught
# on the day it appears rather than at the next audit.
#
# SCOPE — read this before adding a line. The probe runs a NON-PRIVILEGED `lsof`
# as uid 501 (read-only on pico, always, no sudo), so it sees only pico's own
# listeners. Root-owned ones are invisible to it BY CONSTRUCTION and must not be
# listed, or they will read as permanently GONE: sshd :2222, Screen Sharing
# :5900, kdc :88, multipassd :50051, and tailscaled's serve proxy. Every
# `com.zig.*` service runs in the user domain, which is the set this watches.
#
# Derived from a live read, cross-checked against ~/.agents/infra.md's pico Ports
# section. Where infra.md and the live read disagree the LIVE READ wins here and
# the drift belongs in a bead.

# --- wildcard binds (LAN-reachable — no host firewall) ---------------------
*:53             # limactl — lima usernet DNS
*:4317           # phoenix OTLP collector
*:5218           # colima ssh port-forward — vs14 mapserver
*:5427           # colima ssh port-forward — vs14 admin
*:5432           # postgres@17 (the vacation_station database vs14d backs up)
*:7378           # picod-proxy — INTENTIONAL: homeowner ha-portal at
#                  http://pico.local:7378 -> zig-computer:19632
*:8087           # colima ssh port-forward — vs14 cdn
*:14829          # go-jamming webmention receiver
*:15001          # agentgateway MCP
*:15003          # agentgateway LLM
*:17017          # agentgateway claude -> api.anthropic.com relay (no apiKey
#                  policy; transparent passthrough). The fleet's Claude Code
#                  traffic flows through this one — its absence is an outage.

